# AWS-0132 — S3 backups bucket uses SSE-S3 (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key.
#   Why accepted: the LocalStack instance this project provisions against does not run KMS, and
#   SSE-KMS on a bucket without KMS breaks every write (seen in Homework 17's S3 lab).
#   Data is still encrypted at rest. Real AWS: switch to aws_kms_key + sse_algorithm "aws:kms".
#   Review by: 2026-12-31
AWS-0132
